## Split by cause, not by the words in the subject

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Parser: day-first input reaches a month-first shared parser

The shared parser reads month first, although the tenant writes day first. For example, report
`R-41203` describes 2 December becoming 12 February. In the supplied model this is the parser path:
`02/12/2026` is intended as 2 December but read as 12 February.

Use the tenant's date convention or an unambiguous date representation at the parser interface.
Check both app/email traffic and the booking form whose hint already agrees with the tenant.
A parser change alone does not correct the separate form-hint defect.

### Hint: booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to enter month first

The booking-v3 hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY`; its form reads the value in the tenant's day-first convention.
A person following that hint can therefore submit the opposite date even when the form parser follows
the locale. Report `R-41241` describes 6 August becoming 8 June: following the hint gives `08/06/2026`,
which the German tenant's form reads as 8 June.

Make the hint agree with the form's actual parsing convention. Keep this ticket separate from the
shared parser work: form channel plus booking-v3 is the discriminator, not the browser locale.
These examples are scenarios implied by the exported cause model, not executions of product code.

<Review4471 />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## The triage rule disagrees with the working comparison

[Accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and the
[triage prose](/kb/triage/dedupe) merge by normalized subject alone and say uncertainty should be merged.
Both were last reviewed in June 2024; the shared page frame flags them as stale. The comparison below
already uses tenant, locale, form and channel to compare causes instead.

<DedupeExplorer />

The concrete counterexamples matter: Alder form versus app has the same subject but different causes;
Copper versus Morrow form traffic has the same subject/channel but different causes; Pale versus Alder
form traffic can have different subjects yet the same hint cause. An unknown tenant has no known cause,
so identical wording is not enough to merge it.

Proposed replacement practice: resolve tenant and path, compare the demonstrated failure mechanism,
and merge only matching causes. Keep uncertain reports for investigation. Do not silently rewrite the
accepted historical decision; a policy owner must accept a superseding record before this recommendation
becomes the desk's approved policy.

## Desk action and verification limits

- Track parser and hint separately, preserving unique report IDs and the disputed one-day wording.
- The corresponding local issue drafts are `issues/parser.md` and `issues/hint.md`. GitHub publication
  is pending the student's manual action; no public ticket or shipped fix is claimed here.
- Before release acceptance, reproduce each input path in the actual product and confirm the hint,
  parser and generated invite agree on the intended date. Recheck the one-day reports individually.
- Refresh the desk export before submission and reconcile additions or changed tenant facts. Do not
  carry these snapshot counts forward as a claim about a newer export.

